2 Manual Provenance And Contributions
*************************************

This manual began as the second-edition Emacspeak user manual and still
contains selected chapters from that project.  Emacsvox-specific
operating guidance, names, requirements, and generated command reference
are maintained in this repository.  Historical chapters retain Emacspeak
terminology where that identity and period context matter.

* Menu:

* Contributing: Contributing.
* Authoring Guidelines: Authoring Guidelines.
* Credits: Credits.


File: emacsvox.info,  Node: Contributing,  Next: Authoring Guidelines,  Up: Announce

2.1 How To Contribute To This Manual
====================================

The Texinfo chapters live under ‘info/’; the current project overview
and installation summary live in ‘Readme.org’ and ‘etc/install.org’.
Submit changes through the Emacsvox repository at
<https://github.com/bartbunting/emacsvox>.  Read ‘AGENTS.md’ before
building or testing: Emacsvox requires Emacs 31 or newer and
repository-local ‘local.mk’ selects the compiler used by supported
targets.

   Do not hand-edit generated references.  ‘info/docs.texi’ and
‘info/keys.texi’ come from the source documentation generator;
‘etc/aural-presentation-reference.org’ comes from
‘utils/emacsvox-aural-audit.el’.


File: emacsvox.info,  Node: Authoring Guidelines,  Next: Credits,  Prev: Contributing,  Up: Announce

2.2 Authoring Guidelines
========================

Keep current operating instructions separate from historical accounts.
State which back end or platform a procedure applies to, avoid
duplicating detailed protocol contracts across repositories, and link to
the owning document.  Validate Texinfo changes with ‘makeinfo’;
regenerate and commit the installed ‘emacsvox.info’ files when the
manual changes.


