12.4 emacsvox
=============

Emacsvox extends Emacs to be a fully functional audio desktop.  This is
the main emacsvox module.  It actually does very little:
   • It sets up Emacs to load package-specific Emacsvox modules as and
     when a package is loaded.
   • It implements function emacsvox which loads the rest of the system.
   • It provides affordances for setting up consistent behavior in
     programming modes.

12.4.1 Emacsvox Commands
------------------------

12.4.1.1 soundscape
...................

 -- Command: soundscape (scape)
     ‘C-. s’
     ‘C-x @ s s’

     Play soundscape.

     (fn SCAPE)

12.4.1.2 soundscape-kill
........................

 -- Command: soundscape-kill

     Stop all running soundscapes.

12.4.1.3 soundscape-stop
........................

 -- Command: soundscape-stop (scape)

     Stop running Soundscape.

     (fn SCAPE)

12.4.2 emacsvox Options
-----------------------

 -- Variable: User Option emacsvox-pip-enable
     Load pip if Piper-TTS is available.

     Default Value:

     nil


 -- Variable: User Option soundscape-data
     Soundscape data directory.

     Default Value:

     "~/.boodler/Collection"


 -- Variable: User Option soundscape-device
     Alsa sound device to use for soundscapes.

     Default Value:

     "default"


 -- Variable: User Option soundscape-manager-options
     User customizable options list passed to boodler.
     Defaults specify alsa as the output and set master volume

     Default Value:

     ("-o" "pulse" "-m" "0.15")



