12.15 emacsvox-aural
====================

This module owns the device-independent vocabulary used by Aural
Presentation.  It deliberately contains no speech-server, sound player,
major-mode, or resource resolution.

12.15.1 Emacsvox-Aural Commands
-------------------------------

12.15.1.1 emacsvox-aural-toggle-face-presentation
.................................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-aural-toggle-face-presentation (&optional arg)

     Toggle explicit visual-face presentation.

     With a positive prefix ARG, enable it.  With zero or a negative prefix,
     disable it.  This does not change semantic presentation or Voice Lock.

     (fn &optional ARG)

12.15.2 emacsvox-aural Options
------------------------------

 -- Variable: User Option emacsvox-aural-face-presentation-enabled
     Whether rules selected by explicit visual faces participate.

     This control affects rules with a ‘:legacy-face’ selector.  It does not
     disable semantic role, state, event, or attribute presentation, and it does
     not replace ‘voice-lock-mode’.  Voice Lock continues to control only the
     legacy face/personality-to-voice compatibility mapping.

     Default Value:

     t



File: emacsvox.info,  Node: emacsvox-aural-compatibility-voice,  Next: emacsvox-aural-compiler,  Prev: emacsvox-aural,  Up: Emacsvox Commands And Options

12.16 emacsvox-aural-compatibility-voice
========================================

Aural-facing control over the per-buffer legacy face and personality
voice adapter.  Voice Lock remains the compatibility implementation
while aural presentation owns the user-facing policy.

12.16.1 Emacsvox-Aural-Compatibility-Voice Commands
---------------------------------------------------

12.16.1.1 emacsvox-aural-toggle-compatibility-voice
...................................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-aural-toggle-compatibility-voice (&optional arg
          buffer)

     Toggle legacy compatibility voices in BUFFER.

     With a positive prefix ARG, enable them.  With zero or a negative prefix,
     disable them.  This does not change semantic presentation or explicit
     visual-face presentation rules.

     (fn &optional ARG BUFFER)

12.16.1.2 voice-lock-mode
.........................

 -- Command: voice-lock-mode (&optional arg)
     ‘C-e d v’

     Toggle the legacy face and personality voice compatibility adapter.

     This is a minor mode.  If called interactively, toggle the ‘Voice-Lock
     mode’ mode.  If the prefix argument is positive, enable the mode, and if
     it is zero or negative, disable the mode.

     If called from Lisp, toggle the mode if ARG is ‘toggle’.  Enable the
     mode if ARG is nil, omitted, or is a positive number.  Disable the mode
     if ARG is a negative number.

     To check whether the minor mode is enabled in the current buffer,
     evaluate the variable ‘voice-lock-mode’.

     The mode’s hook is called both when the mode is enabled and when it is
     disabled.

     (fn &optional ARG)

12.16.1.3 voice-lock-mode-turn-on
.................................

 -- Command: voice-lock-mode--turn-on

     Turn on the Voice Lock compatibility adapter.

12.16.2 emacsvox-aural-compatibility-voice Options
--------------------------------------------------

 -- Variable: User Option voice-lock-mode-hook
     Hook run after entering or leaving ‘voice-lock-mode’.
     No problems result if this variable is not bound.
     ‘add-hook’ automatically binds it.  (This is true for all hook variables.)

     Default Value:

     (emacsvox-aural--voice-lock-mode-changed voice-lock-mode--set-explicitly)



File: emacsvox.info,  Node: emacsvox-aural-compiler,  Next: emacsvox-aural-concrete,  Prev: emacsvox-aural-compatibility-voice,  Up: Emacsvox Commands And Options

12.17 emacsvox-aural-compiler
=============================

Compile resolved render plans to frozen resources, voices, spatial
values, and backend-ready ordered actions.  This module performs no
queueing or speech-server process control.

12.17.1 emacsvox-aural-compiler Options
---------------------------------------

 -- Variable: User Option emacsvox-aural-unsupported-volume-policy
     Policy for explicit volume when the active transport cannot apply it.

     ‘degrade’ queues the presentation without volume and records the exact
     capability degradation.  ‘reject’ signals an error before anything is queued.

     Default Value:

     degrade



File: emacsvox.info,  Node: emacsvox-aural-concrete,  Next: emacsvox-aural-description,  Prev: emacsvox-aural-compiler,  Up: Emacsvox Commands And Options

12.18 emacsvox-aural-concrete
=============================

Data-only records shared by concrete compilation, queue transport,
descriptions, inspection, and history.  This module owns no rule
resolution, resource lookup, TTS policy, or backend calls.


File: emacsvox.info,  Node: emacsvox-aural-description,  Next: emacsvox-aural-doctor,  Prev: emacsvox-aural-concrete,  Up: Emacsvox Commands And Options

12.19 emacsvox-aural-description
================================

Pure, reusable descriptions of aural values, selectors, rules, and
concrete actions for spoken managers, editors, and explanation buffers.


