File: emacsvox.info,  Node: emacsvox-aural-voice-workbench,  Next: emacsvox-avy,  Prev: emacsvox-aural-voice-palettes,  Up: Emacsvox Commands And Options

12.53 emacsvox-aural-voice-workbench
====================================

A single accessible workbench presents logical voices, physical
inventory, engines, and portable style/effect information.
Transactional previews use the same sample text without changing saved
palettes or routing profiles.

12.53.1 Emacsvox-Aural-Voice-Workbench Commands
-----------------------------------------------

12.53.1.1 emacsvox-aural-prefer-engine
......................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-aural-prefer-engine (engine-id &optional save)
     ‘C-e d e’

     Prefer ENGINE-ID globally while preserving explicit voice routes.

     By default the change lasts for this Emacs session.  With prefix argument
     SAVE, atomically save it in the active routing profile.  Remaining engines
     keep their relative order; explicit logical-voice routes and fallback policy
     are unchanged.  The command does not stop speech already playing.

     (fn ENGINE-ID &optional SAVE)

12.53.1.2 emacsvox-aural-restore-saved-engine-order
...................................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-aural-restore-saved-engine-order

     Clear the temporary engine preference and reapply the saved order.

